   "caption": "Pretreated feed arrives softened and free of chlorine and chloramine. A heat exchanger brings winter feed up to membrane design temperature. The first RO pass removes most dissolved ions, organics, particles and bacteria. Carbon dioxide passes RO as a gas, so we convert it with caustic dosing or strip it with a membrane degasser before it loads the EDI. A second RO pass, where your feed needs one, adds margin on conductivity and silica. EDI polishes the permeate in an electric field, with no acid or caustic regeneration. Water below the conductivity setpoint goes to storage; anything above it diverts until it recovers."
